diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the HTTP application layer on the internal web server. The Apache HTTP Server (apache2) daemon on srv1 is stopped, so no web service is available on port 80.

Mechanism: Client PCs resolve campus names correctly to 10.5.0.4 (srv1) via DNS, but when they try to connect over HTTP the TCP connection fails because nothing is listening on port 80. Browsers often summarize this as “site can’t be found,” which can be mistaken for a DNS issue.

Localization: srv1 (10.5.0.4, interface eth0) hosts both DNS and the web content for the jeremysitlab.com campus zone. Evidence:
- DNS is healthy: from pc1, getent hosts srv1.jeremysitlab.com and www.jeremysitlab.com both return 10.5.0.4; ping to 10.5.0.4 succeeds; s
